# Reported from a playtest: Ajani did not transform when the Cat token died blocking. He does. The Cat token is
# the only other Cat on the battlefield, it dies to a blocker's damage on the opponent's turn, and "whenever one or
# more other Cats you control die" offers the exile-and-return; accepting returns him as the planeswalker.
#
# The choice itself is pictured by ajanis-dying-cat-token-hands-over-the-transform-choice.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains x4
Ajani, Nacatl Pariah
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x4
Fanatic of Rhonas
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ajani, Nacatl Pariah.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Fanatic of Rhonas.Cast
[T6 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Fanatic of Rhonas > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Cat Warrior Token > Fanatic of Rhonas)
Bot1.Accept

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Plains; Ajani, Nacatl Avenger
Bot1.Life = 20
